  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 146 PM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nA period of unsettled weather will arrive Wednesday as a compact \nshort-wave, currently over the Northern Plains, moves across the \nregion. WAA ahead of the main short-wave will kick off a round of \nlight rain showers early Wednesday morning, mainly across northern \nWI. Rainfall amounts are forecast to be around a tenth or two which \nwon't do much to improve the on-going drought across northern WI. \nBehind the upper-shortwave a surface cold front will sweep across \nthe region brining additional rain showers to much of the region at \ntimes through mid Wednesday afternoon. Behind the front winds will \nbecome northerly leading to a prolong period of lake effect \nrain/snow showers across the typical northern WI snowbelt as well as \nalong the Lake Michigan shoreline, especially northern Door Co. \nWhile most areas won't see any accumulating snow, parts of northern \nVilas Co. do have a 50-60% chance for see more than 0.5\" of snow by \nThursday night. As the low and mid levels winds weaken and begin to \nback around to the west Friday these lake effect snow/rain showers \nwill come to an end leaving mostly dry conditions across the region \nfor this weekend. \n\nTemperatures will see a return to near or slightly below normal with \nthe influx of cooler air, with highs in the upper 30s to 40s \nThursday and Friday before gradually trending above normal over the \nweekend.",
